---
config:
  themeCSS: ".warn text { stroke: none !important; } .edgeLabel rect { opacity: 1 !important; fill: #ffffff !important; }"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  accTitle: A MutexRunConfig run as the mutexrunconfig role drives it
  accDescr: The phases of a MutexRunConfig run as the mutexrunconfig role drives them, from the first reconcile to the end of the run or the finalizer, with the task file and the trigger on each transition, including where a failure keeps the pools paused and where nothing is protected.

  state "Ignored" as Ignored
  Ignored : main.yml ends the play
  Ignored : Reconciled=False NamespaceNotAllowed

  state "No run" as Idle
  Idle : 01 and 02 pass, no target node behind
  Idle : and none with this run's released-by
  Idle : main.yml runs 08 as a cleanup pass
  Idle : UpgradeAvailable=False UpgradeUnavailable

  state "Not protecting (fail-open)" as FailOpen
  FailOpen : 01 or 02 failed while nothing is held
  FailOpen : main.yml skips 03 to 08
  FailOpen : Degraded=False NoPoolsPaused
  FailOpen : MCO upgrades the nodes WITHOUT Jobs

  state "Run: pools held (fail-closed)" as Run {
    state "Holding" as Holding
    Holding : 03 paused the target pools (paused-by)
    Holding : 04 gave the nodes behind their mutex
    Holding : labels and labelled-by, and the
    Holding : holders the release label
    Holding : MutexRulesApplied=True

    state "Settling" as Settling
    Settling : the canary has the hold selector
    Settling : and release-labelled-at, 05 defers
    Settling : MCPUpdated=False CanaryMembersLabelled

    state "Re-pointed, armed" as Armed
    Armed : canary + release In (v)
    Armed : target pools + release NotIn (v)
    Armed : MCPUpdated=True UpdateSucceeded
    Armed : UpgradeReady=False, so 06 does not run

    state "Processing node i of n" as Processing
    Processing : main.yml sets JobRun and loops 06
    Processing : released nodes, in-flight nodes, the rest
    Processing : 07 runs each pre and cleanup Job
    Processing : JobRun, NodeUpgrade "Node is i of n"

    Holding --> Settling : 04 stamped the canary, 05 defers
    Holding --> Armed : no stamp, 05 re-points at once
    Settling --> Armed : 05, a reconcile 300 s or more after the stamp
    Armed --> Processing : 02 reads history[0] Completed (UpgradeReady)
    Processing --> Processing : 06, the next node
  }

  state "Failed, holding (fail-closed)" as Failed
  Failed : a rescue set mutexrunconfig_failure
  Failed : later steps and 08 are skipped,
  Failed : nothing is unpaused
  Failed : Degraded=True PoolsLeftPaused
  Failed : retried with backoff

  state "Restoring" as Restore
  Restore : 08 restores the target pools, the canary last
  Restore : removes the mutex labels and node marks
  Restore : unpauses the pools with its paused-by
  Restore : MCPUpdated=False SelectorsRestored
  Restore : UpgradeAvailable=False UpgradeFinished

  state "Restored, sweep pending" as Sweep
  Sweep : the canary has restored-at
  Sweep : the canary's own nodes keep the
  Sweep : release label, no pool selects on it

  state "Finalizing" as Finalizing
  Finalizing : on delete, from any state
  Finalizing : main.yml runs 00 and 08, not 09
  Finalizing : one pass, release labels go at once
  Finalizing : the remaining nodes upgrade
  Finalizing : WITHOUT Jobs

  [*] --> Ignored : outside POD_NAMESPACE
  [*] --> Idle : first reconcile in the namespace
  Idle --> FailOpen : 01 or 02 fails
  FailOpen --> Idle : cause fixed, retry
  Idle --> Holding : 02 finds a node behind, main.yml runs 03 and 04
  Run --> Failed : a step from 01 to 07 fails
  Failed --> Run : retry, the labels and annotations show where it stopped
  Processing --> Restore : last node done, JobRun still true
  Restore --> Failed : 08 fails
  Failed --> Restore : retry, no node behind
  Restore --> Sweep : a node still has the release label
  Restore --> Idle : no node has the release label
  Sweep --> Idle : 08, a reconcile 300 s or more after restored-at
  Run --> Finalizing : delete, 06 stops before the next node
  Failed --> Finalizing : delete
  Finalizing --> Finalizing : a task failed, the finalizer stays, retry
  Finalizing --> [*] : no task failed, ansible-operator removes the finalizer

  classDef warn fill:#fde2e1,stroke:#b42318,color:#000000
  class FailOpen warn
  class Finalizing warn
